(room *(vignette $))

%% Where the divination first places you
#n-ziqqurat
(name *) ziggurat
(room *)
(* has coordinates [3 3 2])
(look *)
	(select)
		Everything is a haze. Colors muted, sounds muffled. But you can make out one line, and then another, and another—something solid, something (emph {real}). You try to focus your mind on it, and a shape begins to emerge. The fog recedes in a great rush and a ringing silence fills your ears.
		(pause)
	(or)
	(stopping)
	
	You’re standing on a wide platform halfway up a tower of towers: one massive pillar stacked on another, on another, on another. The top vanishes into the mists above and the ground is nothing but a distant blur. You’re left on the walkway in between, canted at a steeper angle than is really comfortable. (par)
	
	All around, other memories have forced their way in like tree roots cracking through a sidewalk. To the south, the walkway runs headlong into the front of a mud-brick house, its (vlink {door})
	(if) (#door is open) (then)
		standing open
	(elseif) (#door is openable) (then)
		loosely closed
	(else)
		firmly barred from the other side
	(endif)
	; west, the steps down barely make it a meter before
	(if) ~(statue is turned) (then)
		they’re lost in a (vlink {blinding light})
	(else)
		turning into a trampled hallway
	(endif)
	(if) (#m-unfinished is visited) (then)
		; and some new (vlink {construction}) intrudes from the north
	(endif)
	.
	
	(if) (#n-execution is unvisited) (then)
		(par) The whole tableau is frozen, unmoving, like a fly trapped in amber. The dust swirls around your feet with every step, but the moment you’re past, it hangs motionless in the air. The only flicker of movement is along the walkway to the northwest.
	(else)
		The whole tableau is frozen, unmoving, like a fly trapped in amber.
	(endif)

(from * go #down to #west)
(from * go #west through #light to #n-workshop) ~(statue is turned)
(from * go #west to #n-workshop) (statue is turned)
(from * go #south through #door to #n-home)

(from * go #northwest to #n-execution)

